---

<Layout title="Drylining Leith | Partition Walls &amp; Ceilings Contractors" description="Professional drylining contractors in Leith. Expert partition walls, suspended ceilings, and plasterboard installation for Leith, The Shore, and the wider EH6 postcode region. Free quotes." canonical="/areas/leith/" schema={schema}>
  <section style="position:relative;min-height:400px;display:flex;align-items:center;background:linear-gradient(135deg,#1a1a2e 0%,#16213e 100%);overflow:hidden;"> <img src="/images/hero-main.jpg" alt="Drylining services in Leith and The Shore" style="position:absolute;inset:0;width:100%;height:100%;object-fit:cover;opacity:0.25;"> <div class="container" style="position:relative;z-index:1;text-align:center;padding:60px 20px;"> <nav style="font-size:13px;color:rgba(255,255,255,0.70);margin-bottom:12px;"> <a href="/" style="text-decoration:none;color:rgba(255,255,255,0.70);">Home</a> / <a href="/areas/" style="text-decoration:none;color:rgba(255,255,255,0.70);">Areas</a> / <span style="color:#ffffff;">Drylining in Leith</span> </nav> <h1 style="font-size:clamp(28px,4vw,44px);font-weight:800;color:#ffffff;margin-bottom:14px;line-height:1.15;">Drylining in Leith</h1> <p style="font-size:17px;color:rgba(255,255,255,0.85);max-width:700px;margin:0 auto;line-height:1.6;">CSCS-accredited drylining contractors delivering partition walls, suspended ceilings, and plasterboard across Leith, The Shore, and the wider EH6 postcode region.</p> </div> </section> <section class="section"><div class="container" style="max-width:900px;"> <div style="padding:24px;margin-bottom:24px;border-left:4px solid var(--primary);background:var(--white);border-radius:var(--radius);border:1px solid var(--border);"> <p style="margin:0;font-size:15px;color:var(--text);"><strong>TL;DR:</strong> Drylining Leith provides drylining, partition walls, and suspended ceilings across Leith (EH6), The Shore, and the wider Edinburgh waterfront area. Experienced with Victorian conversions, modern developments, and listed building work.</p> </div> <h2 style="font-size:1.75rem;font-weight:700;color:var(--secondary);margin:2.5rem 0 1rem;">Drylining Services in Leith</h2> <p style="font-size:1.0625rem;color:var(--text);line-height:1.8;margin-bottom:1.5rem;">Leith is Edinburgh's historic waterfront district with a population of over 20,000 in the EH6 postcode area. Home to The Shore, the Water of Leith Walkway, and one of Scotland's most vibrant maritime quarters, the area offers a mix of Victorian terraces, converted warehouses, and large-scale waterfront developments. This diversity means our drylining contractors work on everything from listed warehouse conversions on The Shore to new residential projects at Ocean Terminal and the South Leith regeneration zones.</p> <p style="font-size:1.0625rem;color:var(--text);line-height:1.8;margin-bottom:1.5rem;">The area's major regeneration projects — including the Leith Walk corridor improvements, the Edinburgh Tram extension to Leith, and the ongoing Waterfront developments — create consistent demand for commercial drylining services. We deliver partition wall installation, suspended ceilings, and fire-rated wall systems for office refurbishments, retail units, hospitality venues, and residential developments throughout the EH6 postcode area. All work is carried out to Scottish Building Standards Part H and Part T standards.</p> <h2 style="font-size:1.75rem;font-weight:700;color:var(--secondary);margin:2.5rem 0 1rem;">What We Do in Leith</h2> <p style="font-size:1.0625rem;color:var(--text);line-height:1.8;margin-bottom:1.5rem;">Our Leith crew handles everything from single-room domestic renovations on Great James Street to large-scale commercial fit-outs at Ocean Terminal — covering partition walls, suspended ceilings, and plasterboard installation across the entire EH6 postcode region.</p> <ul style="list-style:disc;padding-left:1.5rem;color:var(--text);line-height:1.8;font-size:1.0625rem;margin-bottom:1.5rem;"> <li><strong>Warehouse conversions</strong> — Internal drylining for converted warehouses on The Shore and Victoria Dock with full compliance to Scottish Building Standards</li> <li><strong>New build handover drylining</strong> — Pre-completion drylining for housing developments in South Leith, Ocean Terminal, and the Leith Walk corridor</li> <li><strong>Commercial fit-outs</strong> — Office refurbs, restaurant conversions, and retail units along Leith Walk, The Shore, and Victoria Dock</li> <li><strong>Fire-rated walls</strong> — Multi-storey residential and commercial buildings require Scottish Building Standards compliance, delivered with full documentation for City of Edinburgh Council building standards</li> <li><strong>Suspended ceilings</strong> — Office refurbs, hospitality venues, and education facilities throughout the Leith area</li> <li><strong>Acoustic partitions</strong> — Residential blocks and hotel conversions near Leith Marina and the Water of Leith Walkway</li> </ul> <h2 style="font-size:1.75rem;font-weight:700;color:var(--secondary);margin:2.5rem 0 1rem;">Areas of Leith We Cover</h2> <ul style="list-style:disc;padding-left:1.5rem;color:var(--text);line-height:1.8;font-size:1.0625rem;margin-bottom:1.5rem;"> <li>Leith Walk and Great James Street (EH6)</li> <li>The Shore and Victoria Dock (EH6)</li> <li>Ocean Terminal and Leith Links (EH6)</li> <li>South Leith and Bruntsfield (EH6)</li> <li>Leith Marina and Newhaven (EH6)</li> <li>Granton Road and Leith Hall Place (EH6)</li> <li>Great King Street and Shore Road (EH6)</li> <li>Albany Road and Leith Walk (EH6)</li> <li>East Leith and The Shore (EH6)</li> <li>West Leith and Portobello Road (EH6)</li> </ul> <h2 style="font-size:1.75rem;font-weight:700;color:var(--secondary);margin:2.5rem 0 1rem;">Leith Building Standards &amp; Planning</h2> <p style="font-size:1.0625rem;color:var(--text);line-height:1.8;margin-bottom:1.5rem;">Leith falls under <strong>City of Edinburgh Council</strong> for building standards and planning. The area contains numerous listed buildings, particularly along The Shore and the Water of Leith Walkway. Many properties are within the <strong>Leith Conservation Area</strong>, meaning any internal structural alterations or external drylining insulation may require listed building consent or planning permission. We work closely with clients, architects, and the council building standards surveyors to ensure every project — from a simple room partition in a Victorian terrace on Great James Street to a large commercial fit-out at Ocean Terminal — is fully compliant with current Scottish Building Standards.</p> <h2 style="font-size:1.75rem;font-weight:700;color:var(--secondary);margin:2.5rem 0 1rem;">Why Choose Us for Leith Projects</h2> <p style="font-size:1.0625rem;color:var(--text);line-height:1.8;margin-bottom:1.5rem;">As an Edinburgh-based drylining team with daily operations across Leith and the waterfront, we understand the area's unique demands. From parking permits for Leith Walk sites to working around The Shore's conservation restrictions and managing tight access on narrow closes, our crew knows the area inside out. All operatives are DBS checked, fully uniformed, and experienced in delivering quality work in Leith's mix of historic and modern properties.</p> <h2 style="font-size:1.75rem;font-weight:700;color:var(--secondary);margin:2.5rem 0 1rem;">Related Services</h2> <div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(180px,1fr));gap:10px;margin-bottom:1.5rem;"> <a href="/services/partition-walls/" style="text-decoration:none;padding:10px 14px;background:var(--white);border-radius:6px;font-size:14px;font-weight:600;border:1px solid var(--border);color:var(--text);">Partition Walls</a> <a href="/services/fire-rated-drylining/" style="text-decoration:none;padding:10px 14px;background:var(--white);border-radius:6px;font-size:14px;font-weight:600;border:1px solid var(--border);color:var(--text);">Fire-Rated Drylining</a> <a href="/services/acoustic-drylining/" style="text-decoration:none;padding:10px 14px;background:var(--white);border-radius:6px;font-size:14px;font-weight:600;border:1px solid var(--border);color:var(--text);">Acoustic Drylining</a> <a href="/services/refurbishment-drylining/" style="text-decoration:none;padding:10px 14px;background:var(--white);border-radius:6px;font-size:14px;font-weight:600;border:1px solid var(--border);color:var(--text);">Refurbishment Drylining</a> </div> <h2 style="font-size:1.75rem;font-weight:700;color:var(--secondary);margin:2.5rem 0 1rem;">Nearby Areas</h2> <ul style="list-style:disc;padding-left:1.5rem;color:var(--text);line-height:1.8;font-size:1.0625rem;margin-bottom:1.5rem;"> <li><a href="/areas/edinburgh/" style="color:var(--primary);text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;">Edinburgh City Centre</a> — 10 minutes via A1</li> <li><a href="/areas/musselburgh/" style="color:var(--primary);text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;">Musselburgh</a> — 15 minutes via A1</li> <li><a href="/areas/livingston/" style="color:var(--primary);text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;">Livingston</a> — 30 minutes via M8</li> <li><a href="/areas/falkirk/" style="color:var(--primary);text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;">Falkirk</a> — 40 minutes via M9</li> </ul> <h2 style="font-size:1.75rem;font-weight:700;color:var(--secondary);margin:2.5rem 0 1rem;">Frequently Asked Questions</h2> <div style="margin-bottom:2rem;"> <div style="border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:var(--radius);overflow:hidden;margin-bottom:1rem;"> <details style="border:none;"> <summary style="width:100%;text-align:left;background:var(--white);border:none;padding:1.25rem 1.5rem;font-size:1rem;font-weight:600;color:var(--secondary);cursor:pointer;display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center;list-style:none;"> What is dry lining and how does it work? <span style="font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--primary);">+</span> </summary> <div style="padding:0 1.5rem;color:var(--text-light);line-height:1.7;font-size:0.9375rem;"> Dry lining is a method of finishing internal walls and ceilings with plasterboard rather than applying several layers of wet plaster. The boards can be fixed directly to brick or blockwork with drywall adhesive, often called the dot and dab method, or screwed to a timber or metal frame. Once the plasterboard is secure, the joints and screw heads are covered with tape and jointing compound. The surface can then be sanded, painted, wallpapered or finished with a thin plaster skim. Dry lining is commonly used in new builds, extensions, renovations and commercial properties. It provides a smooth finish quickly and can also create space for insulation, soundproofing materials, electrical cables and pipework. </div> </details> </div> <div style="border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:var(--radius);overflow:hidden;margin-bottom:1rem;"> <details style="border:none;"> <summary style="width:100%;text-align:left;background:var(--white);border:none;padding:1.25rem 1.5rem;font-size:1rem;font-weight:600;color:var(--secondary);cursor:pointer;display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center;list-style:none;"> Do I need planning permission for drylining in Leith? <span style="font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--primary);">+</span> </summary> <div style="padding:0 1.5rem;color:var(--text-light);line-height:1.7;font-size:0.9375rem;"> Internal drylining usually falls under permitted development rights and doesn't require planning permission. However, if your property is listed (Leith has numerous listed buildings along The Shore and Victoria Dock) or within a Conservation Area, you'll need listed building consent for any internal alterations. We advise checking with City of Edinburgh Council's planning department before starting work on period properties in The Shore or Leith Walk.</div> </details> </div> <div style="border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:var(--radius);overflow:hidden;margin-bottom:1rem;"> <details style="border:none;"> <summary style="width:100%;text-align:left;background:var(--white);border:none;padding:1.25rem 1.5rem;font-size:1rem;font-weight:600;color:var(--secondary);cursor:pointer;display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center;list-style:none;"> What are Scottish Building Standards for drylining? <span style="font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--primary);">+</span> </summary> <div style="padding:0 1.5rem;color:var(--text-light);line-height:1.7;font-size:0.9375rem;"> Scottish Building Standards Part H covers heat and energy efficiency, Part T covers ventilation, and Part C covers structural adequacy. All our drylining work in Leith complies with current Scottish Building Standards. For fire-rated walls, we follow the Fire Standard (Part B) and provide full documentation. We also ensure thermal insulation meets the latest Part H requirements, which is particularly important for Leith's older properties with solid stone walls.</div> </details> </div> <div style="border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:var(--radius);overflow:hidden;margin-bottom:1rem;"> <details style="border:none;"> <summary style="width:100%;text-align:left;background:var(--white);border:none;padding:1.25rem 1.5rem;font-size:1rem;font-weight:600;color:var(--secondary);cursor:pointer;display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center;list-style:none;"> How long does drylining take in Leith? <span style="font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--primary);">+</span> </summary> <div style="padding:0 1.5rem;color:var(--text-light);line-height:1.7;font-size:0.9375rem;"> A typical single-room drylining job takes 2–3 days for framing and board installation, plus 1–2 days for taping, jointing, and sanding. Larger commercial projects at Ocean Terminal or along Leith Walk can take 1–4 weeks depending on scale. We work efficiently to minimise disruption, especially on listed building projects along The Shore where access can be tight.</div> </details> </div> <div style="border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:var(--radius);overflow:hidden;margin-bottom:1rem;"> <details style="border:none;"> <summary style="width:100%;text-align:left;background:var(--white);border:none;padding:1.25rem 1.5rem;font-size:1rem;font-weight:600;color:var(--secondary);cursor:pointer;display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center;list-style:none;"> Do you offer free quotes for Leith projects? <span style="font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--primary);">+</span> </summary> <div style="padding:0 1.5rem;color:var(--text-light);line-height:1.7;font-size:0.9375rem;"> Yes, we offer free, no-obligation site visits and written quotes for all drylining projects across Leith and the wider Edinburgh area. We'll assess your property, discuss your requirements, and provide a detailed written quote within 48 hours. Call us on 0800 820 3090 or fill in our contact form to arrange your free site visit.</div> </details> </div> </div> <h2 style="font-size:1.75rem;font-weight:700;color:var(--secondary);margin:2.5rem 0 1rem;">Get a Free Leith Quote</h2> <p style="font-size:1.0625rem;color:var(--text);line-height:1.8;margin-bottom:2rem;">We offer free, no-obligation site visits and written quotes for all drylining projects across Leith. Call us or fill in our quick form.</p> <div style="margin-top:2rem;text-align:center;"> <a href="/get-quote/" class="btn btn-primary" style="font-size:1.0625rem;padding:1rem 2.5rem;">Get a Free Leith Quote</a> <a href="tel:08008203090" class="btn btn-secondary" style="font-size:1.0625rem;padding:1rem 2.5rem;border:2px solid var(--primary);background:transparent;color:var(--primary);margin-left:0.5rem;">FREEPHONE 0800 820 3090</a> </div> </div></section>
</Layout>
